NS_InvokeByIndex hardcodes the LP64 vtable layout: an 8 byte slot stride, an
8 byte load of the vtable pointer and an 8 byte indirect call through memory.
On x32 the vtable pointer and every slot are 4 bytes, so the 8 byte load picks
up the following object member as the high half of the vtable address and the
call faults. Segfault seen in every XPConnect call into native code.

--- firefox-153.0/xpcom/reflect/xptcall/md/unix/xptcinvoke_asm_x86_64_unix.S.vanilla
+++ firefox-153.0/xpcom/reflect/xptcall/md/unix/xptcinvoke_asm_x86_64_unix.S
@@ -96,9 +96,18 @@ SYM(NS_InvokeByIndex):
   add rsp, 112
 
 # load the function pointer and call
+#ifdef __ILP32__
+# On x32 the vtable pointer and every vtable slot are 4 bytes wide, and an
+# indirect call through memory would read 8, so load the target explicitly.
+  lea eax, [r13d * 4]
+  add eax, [rdi]
+  mov eax, [eax]
+  call rax
+#else
   lea eax, [r13d * 8]
   add rax, [rdi]
   call [rax]
+#endif
 
 # r12 and r13 were pushed relative to the old stack pointer which is now the
 # frame pointer.


InvokeCopyToStack() widens each XPCOM argument into the uint64_t gpregs[]
array that NS_InvokeByIndex later loads into rsi/rdx/rcx/r8/r9 with full
64 bit moves.  Pointers are widened with a plain (uint64_t) cast, which on
x32 is a cast from a 32 bit pointer to a wider integer: gcc emits movslq and
sign extends.  Any pointer at or above 0x80000000 therefore reaches the
callee as 0xffffffffxxxxxxxx and faults on first dereference.

x32 puts the stack near the top of the 4 GB address space (0xfff5c000) and
maps libxul plus the malloc arenas well above 2 GB, so both the indirect
case (&s->val, typically stack) and the T_CHAR_STR / T_INTERFACE default
case are hit in practice.  Firefox segfaults during startup in strlen(),
called from nsTSubstring::Assign(const char*, size_type(-1)) on a "utf-8"
charset string passed through xptcall.

Casting via uintptr_t makes the widening a zero extension, and also drops
the -Wpointer-to-int-cast warning gcc emits here.

--- firefox-153.0/xpcom/reflect/xptcall/md/unix/xptcinvoke_x86_64_unix.cpp.vanilla
+++ firefox-153.0/xpcom/reflect/xptcall/md/unix/xptcinvoke_x86_64_unix.cpp
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ InvokeCopyToStack(uint64_t * gpregs, dou
 
     for (uint32_t i = 0; i < paramCount; i++, s++) {
         if (s->IsIndirect())
-            value = (uint64_t) &s->val;
+            value = (uint64_t)(uintptr_t) &s->val;
         else {
             switch (s->type) {
             case nsXPTType::T_FLOAT:                                break;
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@ InvokeCopyToStack(uint64_t * gpregs, dou
             case nsXPTType::T_BOOL:   value = s->val.b;             break;
             case nsXPTType::T_CHAR:   value = s->val.c;             break;
             case nsXPTType::T_WCHAR:  value = s->val.wc;            break;
-            default:                  value = (uint64_t) s->val.p;  break;
+            default:                  value = (uint64_t)(uintptr_t) s->val.p; break;
             }
         }
 


